{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Security - Events - Okta Security Threat Detected",
	"Description": "Okta ThreatInsight flagged the request as a threat. Okta scores requests against traffic it sees across every tenant, so this fires on addresses already implicated in credential attacks elsewhere.\n\nEvent types: security.threat.detected, security.request.blocked\n\nReference(s):\n- https://help.okta.com/en-us/content/topics/security/threat-insight/okta-threatinsight-overview.htm\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "a903986e-1479-541a-9f0d-f85272658bf0",
